A8  PARTIAL (first half)
    A logged-out opencode became a terminal-family session, and it DECLARED IT:
      condition=undefined  requestedDriverId=opencode-server -> driverId=generic-pty
      accounts.list loginRequired=true
    So this is NOT POD-2772's silent demotion: the demotion is recorded as
    requested-versus-actual, the session carries a typed condition, and the
    account readout asks for a login. Degrading to the terminal path so an
    interactive login is possible is the documented behaviour.

    What is NOT there is a login AFFORDANCE on the session itself:
      interactions.list = empty — nothing offers to log you in
    The catalogue already declares this: login(harness, method) as a utility
    session is ABSENT, and logout/exportCredential/seedCredential are missing
    from the contract entirely (section 12). PARTIAL rather than PASS because
    the row asks for a WORKING login path and there is a declaration, not a path.

    SECOND HALF — "after login, the next session lands on the server driver"
    NOT DRIVEN, and not counted either way. These harnesses authenticate by
    OAuth against live accounts. Performing a login from this drive would
    either mint credentials the rig must not mint, or ROTATE the operator's
    own token and log them out of their daily driver mid-release. The epic
    declined that trade once already, in writing, for claude; declining it
    again here rather than reporting an untested half as passing.
